{{template "top.gohtml" .}}

<h1>Mail app — Configuration</h1>
<p><small>MailApp.sendEmail hands every message to the bundled send-only
relay on the compose network — host <code>mailer</code>, port 25, no credentials,
nothing to configure beyond the toggle and the sender address. The relay
delivers straight to recipient MX servers; its DNS checklist (PTR, SPF) lives
in the README. MailApp.read is not supported — the relay is send-only.</small></p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/mail">
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Settings</legend>
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" {{if .Mail.Enabled}}checked{{end}} /> Enable the mail app</label>
    <label>From address <input type="email" name="from" value="{{.Mail.From}}" placeholder="workflows@example.com" autocomplete="off" /></label>
    <p><small>The envelope sender for every sendEmail call. Bounces return here.</small></p>
    <button type="submit">Save mail settings</button>
  </fieldset>
</form>

{{template "bottom.gohtml" .}}
